@*
    Task Center — tabbed layout (P4, standard GRAC grid style)
    Uses the same DOM patterns as Manage.cshtml:
      * pm-tabs / pm-tab-panel for tab shell
      * pm-table-wrap + bare <table> for grids (same CSS as Practice Instances)
      * pm-action-trigger for 3-dot menus
      * pm-pager with pm-button

    Scope change:
      "Gaps" (Practice Instances requiring implementation work) moved
      OUT of Task Center into its own module — see Views/Practice/Partials/gaps.cshtml
      and migration 050. Task Center is now purely for TASKS:
        * Implementation Tasks (workflow-driven)
        * Assurance Tasks       (workflow-driven, placeholder)
        * Custom Tasks          (owner-authored via + New Task)

      The "+ New Task" button creates ONLY Custom tasks (task_type_code =
      'Custom'). Implementation / Assurance tasks are created upstream —
      Implementation tasks via Gap Center's "Add Implementation Task"
      action, Assurance tasks via the assurance subsystem (later phase).
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1>@Model.Title</h1>
        <p>@Model.Description</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel" id="taskCenterUnavailable" hidden>
    <div class="pm-empty">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-flag-checkered pm-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2 id="taskCenterUnavailableTitle">Task Center is not yet enabled for this organization.</h2>
        <p id="taskCenterUnavailableBody">Ask a GRAC Admin to turn on the <code>screen.tasks</code> feature flag in your organization settings.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pm-panel" id="taskCenterRoot" hidden>

    <div class="pm-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Task Center tabs">
        @*
            The note that used to sit here explained why the Assurance
            tab kept the data-tab key "assurance" for deep links. Migration
            255 merged that tab into the one list, so the key is gone and
            the old names are mapped in applyDeepLinkFromHash instead.
        *@
        @*
            Candidates come first because that is the order the work
            actually flows in (BRD §4): a source identifies an action,
            Task Centre validates owner + priority + SLA, and only then
            does an Approved Task exist. Putting the gate after the
            outputs would read backwards.
        *@
        @* Task Candidates tab retired from Task Centre. The candidate
           workflow (BRD §5) still exists in the API + DB -- other
           surfaces raise / accept / reject candidates via their own
           calls -- but Task Centre no longer surfaces the queue here.
           The panel markup + JS below stays for now; nothing renders it
           because no tab reaches it. *@
        @* Migration 255: Implementation / Continuous Assurance / Custom
           collapsed into one Tasks tab with Source as a column and a
           filter. They read the same endpoint and the same eleven
           columns, split only by task type.

           This also retires the reason 253 widened the Custom tab to
           cover 'Rectification': with no type filter on the list, a gap
           remediation task is simply a task with Source = Gap. The
           widening in sp_task_list and sp_task_center_counts is left in
           place -- harmless, and still correct for any caller that does
           pass taskTypeCode=Custom.

           Event Driven Assurance stays its own tab: it is not
           practice_task, it reads the event engine directly. See
           conflict 4 in docs/task-centre-v2.md. *@
        <button role="tab" data-tab="all" class="active" aria-selected="true">Tasks <span class="pm-badge" id="tabCountAll">0</span></button>
        <button role="tab" data-tab="event-driven"                  aria-selected="false">Event Driven Assurance <span class="pm-badge" id="tabCountEventDriven">0</span></button>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="taskFilterOrganization">
            <option value="">All organizations</option>
        </select>
        @* Migration 255. Values are practice_task.source_type_code, which
           sp_task_list already accepts as @source_type_code -- no API or
           procedure change was needed for this filter.

           The list is ck_pm_practice_task_source_type as widened by
           migration 215, exactly: Gap / Exception / Risk / RiskRegister /
           ContinuousAssurance / EventAssurance / Custom. An option that
           is not in that CHECK would be a filter that can never match. *@
        @* Migration 256: options are filled from sp_task_centre_source_counts
           so each carries a count, matching Gap Centre's Source filter.
           The static list below is the fallback shown before the counts
           arrive, and if the endpoint fails — the filter still works
           unlabelled rather than emptying itself. *@
        <select id="taskFilterSource" title="Filter by the module that raised the task">
            <option value="">All sources</option>
            <option value="Gap">Gap</option>
            <option value="Exception">Exception</option>
            <option value="Risk">Risk candidate</option>
            <option value="RiskRegister">Risk register</option>
            <option value="ContinuousAssurance">Continuous Assurance</option>
            <option value="EventAssurance">Event Assurance</option>
            <option value="Custom">Custom</option>
        </select>
        <input id="taskCenterSearch" type="text" placeholder="Search subject / instance / practice..." />
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="taskRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
        <button class="pm-button primary" id="taskAddBtn" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> New Task
        </button>
    </div>

    @* Gaps tab was moved out into its own Gap Center module (see gaps.cshtml + migration 050). *@

    @*
        Task Candidates tab (BRD §5). Identified actions awaiting
        execution validation. Deliberately shows only what this stage
        decides — owner, priority, derived SLA — and never severity or
        impact, which stay with the source.
    *@
    <div class="pm-tab-panel" data-panel="candidates" hidden>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Candidate #</th><th>Action</th><th>Source</th>
                        <th>Proposed Owner</th><th>Priority</th><th>Proposed Due</th>
                        <th>Status</th><th>Actions</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="taskBody-candidates"><tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load candidates.</td></tr></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-pager" data-pager="candidates">
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="prev" type="button">Previous</button>
            <span data-pg="label">Page 1</span>
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="next" type="button">Next</button>
            <span data-pg="total" class="pm-pager-total">0 total</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Migration 255: Implementation / Continuous Assurance / Custom were
       three views of practice_task split by task type, all reading the
       same endpoint with the same eleven columns. One grid now, with
       Source as a column and a filter. Event Driven Assurance keeps its
       own tab below -- it is not practice_task at all, it reads the
       event engine directly (see conflict 4 in docs/task-centre-v2.md).

       Column labels are the generic ones. "Task Name" covered
       implementation and custom already; "Assurance Activity" was the
       same cell under a different heading. *@
    <div class="pm-tab-panel" data-panel="all">
        <div class="pm-table-wrap">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Task #</th><th>Task Name</th><th>Source</th><th>Related Record</th>
                        <th>Assigned To</th><th>Priority</th><th>Target Date</th>
                        <th>SLA Status</th><th>Children</th><th>Status</th><th>Actions</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="taskBody-all"><tr><td colspan="11" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load tasks.</td></tr></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-pager" data-pager="all">
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="prev" type="button">Previous</button>
            <span data-pg="label">Page 1</span>
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="next" type="button">Next</button>
            <span data-pg="total" class="pm-pager-total">0 total</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    @*
        Event Driven Assurance tab. The panel is a partial so there is one
        implementation of the event checklist behaviour, and it reads the
        event engine directly rather than mirroring event_instance rows into
        practice_task -- see the partial's header for why.
    *@
    <div class="pm-tab-panel" data-panel="event-driven" hidden>
        <partial name="Partials/_event-assurance-panel" />
    </div>

</section>

@* Add Implementation Task modal — exposes window.__openAddImplTask *@
<partial name="Partials/_add-implementation-task-modal" model="Model" />

@* Shared Edit / Complete / Close / Add Evidence dialogs -- moved into
   Partials/_task-action-dialogs.cshtml + Shared/task-actions.js
   (window.gracTaskActions) so Task View's own Actions menu can reuse
   these exact forms, API calls, validation and success/error handling
   instead of a second copy, per the change request. See that partial's
   header comment. *@
<partial name="Partials/_task-action-dialogs" />

@* New Task dialog — locked to task_type_code = 'Custom' *@

@* Shared pager (and escape/badge helpers) — exposes window.__wfCommon.
   Self-guards on re-render, so rendering it here is safe even when the
   host page has already pulled it in for another partial. *@
<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />

<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';
    if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
    else init();

    // Published deployments run under a PathBase (e.g. "/Practicemanagement"
    // per appsettings.json). The layout exposes it as window.appBasePath;
    // prepend it to every same-origin fetch so the URL becomes
    // `${basePath}/practice/api/...` -- otherwise the request hits
    // `/practice/api/...` at the origin root and returns 404 in production
    // even though it works locally where PathBase is empty.
    //
    // IMPORTANT: this IIFE runs at script-parse time -- BEFORE the layout's
    // trailing inline script that sets window.pmPathBase. If we captured
    // APP_BASE eagerly here it would always be '' in published builds.
    // Resolve lazily inside U() so the actual fetch URL is computed at call
    // time (which happens on DOMContentLoaded / user interaction -- well
    // after every inline layout script has run).
    const U = p => String(window.appBasePath || window.pmPathBase || '').replace(/\/+$/, '') + p;


    let selectedOrgId = null;
    // Migration 255: 'all' is the merged practice_task list.
    let activeTab     = 'all';
    // 'event-driven' has no pager: sp_event_checklist_inbox_list returns the
    // open set for the organization, not a page.
    let pagesByTab    = { candidates: 1, all: 1 };
    const EVENT_TAB   = 'event-driven';
    const PAGE_SIZE   = 25;
    let searchDebounce = null;
    let openMenuEl      = null;
    let openMenuTrigger = null;

    // ---- Sub-task tree state -----------------------------------------
    // Declared HERE, with the rest of the module state, and not beside
    // the functions that use them: init() is called at script-parse time
    // (see the readyState test at the top of this IIFE), so a `let` in
    // the middle of the file sits in its temporal dead zone during that
    // call. Nothing reaches these before the first fetch resolves today,
    // which is exactly the kind of accident that stops being true later.
    //
    // childRowCache is per parent and is dropped on every grid refresh,
    // so restoring an expansion re-fetches and shows current data.
    // expandedTaskIds SURVIVES the refresh -- it is what the user had
    // open, not what was fetched.
    const childRowCache  = new Map();   // taskId -> rows[]
    let   expandedTaskIds = new Set();  // taskId (string)

    async function init() {
        const orgs = await loadOrgs();
        const root    = document.getElementById('taskCenterRoot');
        const unavail = document.getElementById('taskCenterUnavailable');
        if (!orgs.length) {
            unavail.hidden = false;
            document.getElementById('taskCenterUnavailableTitle').textContent = 'No organizations are available for your account.';
            document.getElementById('taskCenterUnavailableBody').textContent  = 'Ask a GRAC Admin to map your account to an organization.';
            return;
        }
        root.hidden = false;
        populateOrgSelect(orgs);
        document.getElementById('taskFilterOrganization').addEventListener('change', onOrgChange);
        document.getElementById('taskRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', reloadCurrentTab);
        document.getElementById('taskAddBtn').addEventListener('click', openNewTaskDialog);
        document.getElementById('taskCenterSearch').addEventListener('input', function () {
            clearTimeout(searchDebounce);
            searchDebounce = setTimeout(function () { pagesByTab[activeTab] = 1; reloadCurrentTab(); }, 300);
        });
        // Migration 255: Source replaces the three task-type tabs.
        const srcSel = document.getElementById('taskFilterSource');
        if (srcSel) srcSel.addEventListener('change', function () {
            pagesByTab[activeTab] = 1;
            reloadCurrentTab();
        });
        document.querySelectorAll('.pm-tabs [role="tab"]').forEach(function (btn) {
            btn.addEventListener('click', function () { switchTab(btn.getAttribute('data-tab')); });
        });
        wirePagers();
        window.gracTaskActions.init({
            getOrganizationId: () => selectedOrgId,
            onChanged:         () => { reloadCurrentTab(); refreshCounts(); }
        });
        wireRowMenu();

        // The Event Driven panel reads the organization from Task Center's own
        // selector, so there is one organization control on the screen.
        if (window.__eventAssurance) {
            window.__eventAssurance.init(function () { return selectedOrgId; });
            document.addEventListener('event-assurance:loaded', function (e) {
                const badge = document.getElementById('tabCountEventDriven');
                if (badge) badge.textContent = (e.detail && e.detail.count) || 0;
            });
        }
        applyToolbarForTab();

        // Deep-link support for Gap Center → Task Center hand-off.
        //   Example: /Practice/Index/tasks#tab=implementation&search=INST-001
        // Parse the hash once, apply tab + search, then rely on onOrgChange
        // to fire the actual data load.
        applyDeepLinkFromHash();

        await onOrgChange();
    }

    function applyDeepLinkFromHash() {
        const raw = (window.location.hash || '').replace(/^#/, '');
        if (!raw) return;
        const params = new URLSearchParams(raw);
        const tab = (params.get('tab') || '').toLowerCase();
        const q   = params.get('search') || '';

        // Deep-link support for Gap View → Task Center hand-off (migration
        // 325). #taskId=<id> used to open the task's View dialog directly
        // in-place. The row menu's own "View" action now opens the
        // dedicated Task View full page instead, so this old hash link is
        // redirected there too -- one destination for "View a task",
        // reached by any of the ways into this hash. Anything that still
        // sends #taskId= (an old bookmark, another screen not yet updated)
        // keeps working; it just lands on the better page.
        const taskId = Number(params.get('taskId'));
        if (Number.isFinite(taskId) && taskId > 0) {
            window.location.href = U('/Practice/Index/task-view') + '?taskId=' + encodeURIComponent(taskId);
            return;
        }
        // Migration 255: the old per-type tab names still arrive on
        // deep links from Gap Center and elsewhere. They all mean the one
        // merged list now, so map them onto 'all' rather than 404-ing the
        // link into whatever tab happened to be open.
        const LEGACY_TAB = { implementation: 'all', assurance: 'all', custom: 'all' };
        const mapped = LEGACY_TAB[tab] || tab;
        if (mapped === 'candidates' || mapped === 'all' || mapped === EVENT_TAB) {
            activeTab = mapped;
            document.querySelectorAll('.pm-tabs [role="tab"]').forEach(function (b) {
                const on = b.getAttribute('data-tab') === mapped;
                b.classList.toggle('active', on);
                b.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
            });
            document.querySelectorAll('.pm-tab-panel').forEach(function (p) {
                p.hidden = p.getAttribute('data-panel') !== mapped;
            });
        }
        if (q) {
            const input = document.getElementById('taskCenterSearch');
            if (input) input.value = q;
        }
    }

    async function loadOrgs() {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U('/practice/api/organizations/allowed'), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) return [];
            const b = await r.json();
            const rows = (b && (b.data || b.Data)) || [];
            return rows.map(function (row) {
                return {
                    value: String(row.organizationId || row.OrganizationId || ''),
                    label: String(row.organizationName || row.OrganizationName || '')
                };
            }).filter(function (o) { return o.value; });
        } catch (_) { return []; }
    }
    function populateOrgSelect(orgs) {
        // Unified behavior (Gap Center + Task Center):
        //   * No "Select organization" placeholder -- first permitted
        //     org is auto-selected so records load on initial page.
        //   * Single-org users: dropdown disabled (nothing to switch to).
        //   * Multi-org users: dropdown enabled, change handler reloads.
        //   * Empty list handled upstream in init() (unavailable banner).
        const sel = document.getElementById('taskFilterOrganization');
        sel.innerHTML = '';
        for (const o of orgs) {
            const opt = document.createElement('option');
            opt.value = o.value; opt.textContent = o.label || ('Organization ' + o.value);
            sel.appendChild(opt);
        }
        if (orgs.length > 0) sel.value = orgs[0].value;
        sel.disabled = orgs.length <= 1;
    }
    async function onOrgChange() {
        closeRowMenu();
        selectedOrgId = document.getElementById('taskFilterOrganization').value || null;
        // Migration 255: must match the declaration above. This reset kept
        // the pre-255 shape and wiped the 'all' key on every org change,
        // so loadTasks sent "&page=undefined" and the API rejected the
        // request with HTTP 400 before it ever reached sp_task_list.
        pagesByTab = { candidates: 1, all: 1 };
        // No dialog to refresh here any more: the common Task form loads
        // its assignee list on every open, so an organisation change
        // cannot leave it showing the previous organisation's employees.
        await refreshCounts();
        await reloadCurrentTab();
    }

    async function refreshCounts() {
        if (!selectedOrgId) { setCounts(null); setCandidateCounts(null); return; }
        // Migration 256: the Source options carry counts too, so they are
        // refreshed here rather than at each of refreshCounts' five call
        // sites -- closing a task, creating one and switching org all
        // already come through this function.
        loadTaskSourceFilter();
        const org = encodeURIComponent(selectedOrgId);
        // Two independent endpoints (tasks, candidates) — fetched together
        // so one failing does not blank the other's badge.
        const [tasks, candidates] = await Promise.all([
            fetch(U('/practice/api/tasks/counts?organizationId=') + org, { credentials: 'same-origin' })
                .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; }).catch(function () { return null; }),
            fetch(U('/practice/api/task-candidates/counts?organizationId=') + org, { credentials: 'same-origin' })
                .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; }).catch(function () { return null; })
        ]);
        setCounts(tasks);
        setCandidateCounts(candidates);
    }
    function setCounts(c) {
        // gapsCount intentionally NOT surfaced here — Gap Center owns that
        // metric now. Task Center only shows counts for actual tasks.
        //
        // Migration 255: one badge for the merged list. The counts
        // procedure still returns the three type buckets separately, so
        // they are summed here rather than changing the procedure --
        // Task Center is the only caller that wanted them merged, and
        // sp_task_center_counts is read by other things.
        const badge = document.getElementById('tabCountAll');
        if (badge) {
            badge.textContent = c
                ? ((c.implementationCount || 0) + (c.assuranceCount || 0) + (c.customCount || 0))
                : 0;
        }
    }
    // The Candidates badge counts OPEN candidates (New + Validated) —
    // approved ones already appear as tasks in the other tabs, and
    // discarded ones are history.
    function setCandidateCounts(c) {
        const badge = document.getElementById('tabCountCandidates');
        if (badge) badge.textContent = c ? (c.openCount || 0) : 0;
    }

    function switchTab(tab) {
        closeRowMenu();
        activeTab = tab;
        document.querySelectorAll('.pm-tabs [role="tab"]').forEach(function (b) {
            const on = b.getAttribute('data-tab') === tab;
            b.classList.toggle('active', on);
            b.setAttribute('aria-selected', on ? 'true' : 'false');
        });
        document.querySelectorAll('.pm-tab-panel').forEach(function (p) {
            p.hidden = p.getAttribute('data-panel') !== tab;
        });
        applyToolbarForTab();
        reloadCurrentTab();
    }

    // The Event Driven tab brings its own toolbar (subject filter, Raise
    // Event, Coverage Gaps) inside the partial. The shared task toolbar --
    // search and New Task -- does not apply to it: an event checklist is
    // raised by an event, not typed in as a task.
    function applyToolbarForTab() {
        const isEvent = activeTab === EVENT_TAB;
        const search = document.getElementById('taskCenterSearch');
        const addBtn = document.getElementById('taskAddBtn');
        if (search) search.hidden = isEvent;
        // "+ New Task" creates a CUSTOM task, which by BRD §4B skips the
        // candidate stage entirely — so it has no meaning while the
        // Candidates tab is showing. Candidates are raised by their
        // source, or from the source's own screen.
        if (addBtn) addBtn.hidden = isEvent || activeTab === 'candidates';
    }
    async function reloadCurrentTab() {
        closeRowMenu();
        // THE one place the sub-task cache is dropped.
        //
        // Every write in this screen ends here -- complete, close, edit,
        // add sub task, assign, the governance approvals -- so hooking
        // the cache to this single refresh path is what stops a
        // re-expanded parent showing sub tasks as they were before the
        // action. The alternative, an invalidateChildRows(id) call in
        // each of a dozen handlers, is a dozen chances to forget one.
        invalidateChildRows();
        if (!selectedOrgId) return;
        if (activeTab === 'candidates') return loadCandidates();
        if (activeTab === EVENT_TAB)    return window.__eventAssurance
                                             ? window.__eventAssurance.load()
                                             : undefined;
        // Migration 255: no task-type argument. The list is every
        // practice_task row for the organization; Source is a column and
        // an optional filter rather than three separate fetches.
        return loadTasks();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Task Candidates  (BRD §5)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function loadCandidates() {
        const q = document.getElementById('taskCenterSearch').value.trim();
        const p = pagesByTab.candidates;
        // 'OpenSet' = New + Validated. Approved candidates are visible as
        // tasks; discarded ones are reachable through the source panel.
        const url = U('/practice/api/task-candidates?organizationId=') + encodeURIComponent(selectedOrgId)
                  + '&statusCode=OpenSet'
                  + '&page=' + p + '&pageSize=' + PAGE_SIZE
                  + (q ? '&search=' + encodeURIComponent(q) : '');
        const body = document.getElementById('taskBody-candidates');
        if (body) body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        try {
            const r = await fetch(url, { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
            renderCandidateRows(await r.json());
        } catch (err) {
            if (body) body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">Failed to load: ' + escape(err.message) + '</td></tr>';
        }
    }

    function renderCandidateRows(payload) {
        const body = document.getElementById('taskBody-candidates');
        if (!body) return;
        body.innerHTML = '';
        const rows = (payload && payload.rows) || [];
        if (!rows.length) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty">No candidates awaiting validation.</td></tr>';
        } else {
            for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                const c = rows[i];
                const tr = document.createElement('tr');
                tr.setAttribute('data-candidate-id',    String(c.taskCandidateId));
                tr.setAttribute('data-candidate-state', c.statusCode || '');
                tr.setAttribute('data-candidate-ready', c.isReadyToApprove ? '1' : '0');
                tr.setAttribute('data-candidate-priority', c.proposedPriority || '');
                // Row click-to-View (change request, 2026-09-22): a
                // candidate's "View" is buildCandidateRowMenu()'s own
                // openCandidateView() quick-look modal, not a page -- it
                // has not been validated/approved into a task yet, so
                // there is no Task View for it. Same class as the main
                // list for one consistent cursor affordance; see
                // wireRowMenu() below for what the click actually opens.
                tr.className = 'pm-row-clickable';
                tr.innerHTML = [
                    '<td>' + escape(c.candidateNumber || ('TC-' + c.taskCandidateId)) + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + escape(c.candidateTitle) + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + escape((c.sourceReference || c.sourceTypeCode) + '') + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + candidateOwnerCell(c) + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + escape(c.proposedPriority) + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + candidateDueCell(c) + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + formatBadge(c.statusCode) + '</td>',
                    '<td>' + actionTrigger('candidates', i) + '</td>'
                ].join('');
                body.appendChild(tr);
            }
        }
        updatePager('candidates', payload);
    }

    // An unresolved owner is the single thing blocking approval, so it is
    // called out rather than left blank (BRD §6 rung 7 — manual).
    function candidateOwnerCell(c) {
        if (!c.proposedOwnerEmployeeId)
            return '<span style="color:#b45309;">Needs an owner</span>';
        const src = c.ownerSourceCode && c.ownerSourceCode !== 'MANUAL' && c.ownerSourceCode !== 'EXPLICIT_SOURCE'
            ? '<div style="font-size:11px; color:#64748b;">' + escape(ownerSourceLabel(c.ownerSourceCode)) + '</div>'
            : '';
        return escape(c.proposedOwnerName || c.proposedOwnerEmployeeId) + src;
    }

    function candidateDueCell(c) {
        if (!c.proposedDueAt) return '';
        const note = c.slaSourceCode === 'TYPE_DEFAULT'
            ? '<div style="font-size:11px; color:#64748b;">task-type default</div>' : '';
        return escape(fmtDate(c.proposedDueAt))
             + (c.proposedSlaDays != null ? ' <span style="font-size:11px; color:#64748b;">('
                 + escape(c.proposedSlaDays) + 'd)</span>' : '')
             + note;
    }

    // Migration 255: no taskTypeCode. sp_task_list already treats a NULL
    // @@task_type_code as "every type", and @@source_type_code was already
    // one of its 195 filters -- so the merged list and its Source filter
    // needed no procedure or API change at all.
    //
    // (Those are doubled on purpose. Razor parses an at-sign inside
    // <script> even within a JS comment, so a single one in front of a
    // SQL parameter name compiles as a C# expression and fails with
    // CS0103. Double it to emit one literally.)
    async function loadTasks() {
        const q      = document.getElementById('taskCenterSearch').value.trim();
        const srcEl  = document.getElementById('taskFilterSource');
        const source = srcEl ? (srcEl.value || '') : '';
        const p = pagesByTab.all;
        const url = U('/practice/api/tasks?organizationId=') + encodeURIComponent(selectedOrgId)
                  + '&page=' + p + '&pageSize=' + PAGE_SIZE
                  + (q ? '&search=' + encodeURIComponent(q) : '')
                  + (source ? '&sourceTypeCode=' + encodeURIComponent(source) : '');
        const body = document.getElementById('taskBody-all');
        if (body) body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="11" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        try {
            const r = await fetch(url, { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) {
                // Surface the server's reason rather than the bare status.
                const b = await r.json().catch(function () { return {}; });
                throw new Error(b.error || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
            }
            renderTaskRows('all', await r.json());
        } catch (err) {
            if (body) body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="11" class="pm-empty">Failed to load: ' + escape(err.message) + '</td></tr>';
        }
    }

    // The source_type_code vocabulary from ck_pm_practice_task_source_type
    // (migration 215), mapped to what an operator calls it. An unmapped
    // code falls through as-is rather than rendering blank.
    const TASK_SOURCE_LABELS = {
        Gap:                 'Gap',
        Exception:           'Exception',
        Risk:                'Risk candidate',
        RiskRegister:        'Risk register',
        ContinuousAssurance: 'Continuous Assurance',
        EventAssurance:      'Event Assurance',
        Custom:              'Custom'
    };

    function renderTaskRows(tabKey, payload) {
        const body = document.getElementById('taskBody-' + tabKey);
        if (!body) return;
        body.innerHTML = '';
        const rows = (payload && payload.rows) || [];
        if (!rows.length) {
            body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="11" class="pm-empty">No tasks yet.</td></tr>';
        } else {
            for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                body.appendChild(taskRowEl(rows[i], tabKey, i, 0));
            }
            // WHAT WAS OPEN STAYS OPEN.
            //
            // Every action in this screen ends in reloadCurrentTab(), so
            // without this, completing a sub task would rebuild the grid
            // collapsed and hide the very row the user just acted on --
            // a regression introduced by the tree itself, not something
            // the flat grid could suffer from.
            //
            // Not awaited: each parent's children are an independent
            // fetch, and the grid is already on screen. Ids that are not
            // on this page (the filter or the page moved) are pruned so
            // the set cannot grow without bound.
            restoreExpandedRows(body, tabKey);
        }
        updatePager(tabKey, payload);
    }

    function restoreExpandedRows(body, tabKey) {
        if (!expandedTaskIds.size) return;
        const present = new Set();
        body.querySelectorAll('tr[data-depth="0"]').forEach(function (tr) {
            const id = tr.getAttribute('data-task-id');
            if (!expandedTaskIds.has(id)) return;
            present.add(id);
            const btn = tr.querySelector('.task-tree-toggle[data-task-expand]');
            // No button means the last sub task was removed or completed
            // out of existence -- childCount is 0 now, so there is
            // nothing to reopen and the id drops out below.
            if (btn) toggleTaskRow(btn);
        });
        expandedTaskIds = present;
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // PARENT -> SUB TASK HIERARCHY  (BRD §11, §12)
    //
    // ONE ROW BUILDER, ONE ENDPOINT, ONE ROW MENU. Nothing below is a
    // second implementation of anything:
    //
    //   * The grid list is UNCHANGED. sp_task_list returns top-level
    //     tasks only (`@@include_children = 0` -> `parent_task_id IS
    //     NULL`), so pagination, search, the Source filter, sorting and
    //     the count badges all still describe parent tasks -- exactly as
    //     they did. A sub task never consumes a row of a page.
    //
    //   * Sub tasks come from THE SAME endpoint with `parentTaskId=N`,
    //     which sp_task_list has accepted since 195 ("asking for one
    //     parent's children implies you want children"). The Web proxy
    //     forwards the whole query string, so no controller, no service
    //     and no procedure changed for this.
    //
    //   * Because that returns full TaskListRows, every cell renderer
    //     and every data-task-* attribute is reused verbatim -- which is
    //     what gives each sub task a working 3-dots menu with View,
    //     Complete and Close: buildTaskRowMenu() reads the row it was
    //     clicked on and neither knows nor cares about depth.
    //
    // depth exists so the renderer is not one level deep by accident.
    // The MODEL is one level -- sp_task_child_create throws 55674, "child
    // tasks cannot themselves have children" -- so childCount on a sub
    // task is always 0 and no toggle is drawn. If that rule is ever
    // relaxed, this renders the extra levels without being touched.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const MAX_TREE_DEPTH = 6;   // a guard against a cycle in the data,
                                // not a product limit.

    function taskRowEl(r, tabKey, index, depth) {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-id',       String(r.taskId));
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-state',    r.currentStatusCode || '');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-terminal', r.currentStatusIsTerminal ? '1' : '0');
        // v2 attributes drive the row menu without a second fetch.
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-child',    r.isChild ? '1' : '0');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-eligible', r.isEligibleForCompletion ? '1' : '0');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-priority', r.priority || '');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-due',      r.slaDueAt || '');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-ext',      r.extensionStatusCode || '');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-prio-req', r.priorityChangeStatusCode || '');
        // Migration 255: the row menu used to branch on which tab
        // was open. With one list the type has to travel on the
        // row instead.
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-type',     r.taskTypeCode || '');
        // Read by openAddChildTask() to fill the read-only Parent
        // Task field on the common form -- naming a task the user
        // is already looking at should not need a fetch.
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-number',   r.taskNumber || '');
        tr.setAttribute('data-task-title',    r.subjectTitle || '');
        // ---- tree bookkeeping ----
        // depth positions the row; parent lets collapse find its whole
        // subtree by walking forward while depth is greater than its own.
        tr.setAttribute('data-depth', String(depth));
        if (depth > 0) {
            tr.className = 'task-subrow';
            tr.setAttribute('data-parent-task-id', String(r.parentTaskId || ''));
        }
        // Row click-to-View (change request, 2026-09-22): "View" is
        // unconditional on every task (window.gracTaskActions.buildMenu()
        // offers it with no applicable/disabled gate at all), including a
        // sub task -- each has its own Task View -- so every row gets the
        // clickable class, parent or child alike.
        tr.classList.add('pm-row-clickable');

        const kids = r.childCount || 0;
        tr.innerHTML = [
            '<td>' + treeCell(r, kids, depth, tabKey) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + escape(r.subjectTitle) + pendingBadges(r) + '</td>',
            // Migration 255: Source is the column that replaced
            // the three type tabs. The task type stays visible
            // beneath it -- merging the tabs removed the type as
            // a heading, so the row has to carry it.
            '<td>' + sourceCell(r) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + escape(r.linkedInstanceId ? 'Instance ' + r.linkedInstanceId
                            : (r.subjectEntityType ? r.subjectEntityType + ' ' + r.subjectEntityId : '')) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + ownerCell(r) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + escape(r.priority) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + dueCell(r) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + slaStatusBadge(r) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + childCell(r) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + formatBadge(r.currentStatusName) + '</td>',
            '<td>' + actionTrigger(tabKey, index) + '</td>'
        ].join('');
        return tr;
    }

    // The Task # cell carries the hierarchy: the indent, the branch
    // glyph on a sub task, and the toggle on a parent that has any.
    //
    // A task with NO sub tasks gets a spacer of exactly the toggle's
    // width instead of the toggle, so its number still lines up with the
    // numbers of the parents above and below it. No glyph, no chevron,
    // no hierarchy indicator -- which is what "display it normally" has
    // to mean in a table, where a missing element would shift the column.
    function treeCell(r, kids, depth, tabKey) {
        const num = escape(r.taskNumber || ('T-' + r.organizationId + '-' + r.taskId));
        const pad = depth > 0
            ? '<span class="task-tree-indent" style="width:' + (depth * 18) + 'px"></span>'
              + '<span class="task-tree-branch" aria-hidden="true"></span>'
            : '';
        const toggle = kids > 0 && depth < MAX_TREE_DEPTH
            ? '<button type="button" class="task-tree-toggle" data-task-expand="' + escape(r.taskId) + '"'
              + ' data-tab-key="' + escape(tabKey) + '" data-depth="' + depth + '"'
              + ' aria-expanded="false"'
              + ' title="' + kids + ' sub task' + (kids === 1 ? '' : 's') + '">'
              + '<i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>'
              + '<span class="visually-hidden">Show sub tasks</span>'
              + '</button>'
            : '<span class="task-tree-toggle is-empty" aria-hidden="true"></span>';
        return '<span class="task-tree-cell">' + pad + toggle
             + '<span class="task-tree-num">' + num + '</span></span>';
    }

    // Expand / collapse one parent row.
    //
    // FETCHED ONCE, then cached on the row. Collapsing removes the child
    // rows from the DOM rather than hiding them: they are re-inserted
    // from the cache on the next expand, and a hidden <tr> inside a
    // <tbody> that other code counts is the kind of thing that goes
    // wrong quietly later.
    //
    // Removal walks FORWARD while depth is greater than the parent's,
    // which takes the whole subtree -- a grandchild's rows go with its
    // parent's without this function knowing how deep it went.
    function collapseTaskRow(tr) {
        expandedTaskIds.delete(tr.getAttribute('data-task-id'));
        const depth = Number(tr.getAttribute('data-depth') || 0);
        let n = tr.nextElementSibling;
        while (n && Number(n.getAttribute('data-depth') || 0) > depth) {
            const next = n.nextElementSibling;
            n.remove();
            n = next;
        }
        const btn = tr.querySelector('.task-tree-toggle[data-task-expand]');
        if (btn) {
            btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
            btn.classList.remove('is-open');
        }
    }

    async function toggleTaskRow(btn) {
        const tr = btn.closest('tr');
        if (!tr) return;
        if (btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true') { collapseTaskRow(tr); return; }

        const taskId = btn.getAttribute('data-task-expand');
        const tabKey = btn.getAttribute('data-tab-key') || 'all';
        const depth  = Number(btn.getAttribute('data-depth') || 0);

        let rows = childRowCache.get(String(taskId));
        if (!rows) {
            btn.classList.add('is-busy');
            try {
                // THE SAME LIST ENDPOINT. pageSize 200 is sp_task_list's
                // own ceiling; a work package with more than 200 sub
                // tasks is not a case this grid should paginate inside a
                // row, and the parent's Children column still states the
                // true count.
                const url = U('/practice/api/tasks?organizationId=') + encodeURIComponent(selectedOrgId)
                          + '&parentTaskId=' + encodeURIComponent(taskId)
                          + '&page=1&pageSize=200';
                const resp = await fetch(url, { credentials: 'same-origin' });
                if (!resp.ok) {
                    const b = await resp.json().catch(function () { return {}; });
                    throw new Error(b.error || ('HTTP ' + resp.status));
                }
                const payload = await resp.json();
                rows = (payload && payload.rows) || [];
                childRowCache.set(String(taskId), rows);
            } catch (err) {
                // Reported in the row itself, not an alert: the failure
                // belongs to this one expansion and the rest of the grid
                // is still good.
                const warn = document.createElement('tr');
                warn.className = 'task-subrow';
                warn.setAttribute('data-depth', String(depth + 1));
                warn.innerHTML = '<td colspan="11" class="pm-empty">Sub tasks could not be loaded: '
                               + escape(err.message) + '</td>';
                tr.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', warn);
                btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
                btn.classList.add('is-open');
                return;
            } finally {
                btn.classList.remove('is-busy');
            }
        }

        // Inserted in order directly after the parent. anchor moves so
        // row 2 lands after row 1 rather than all of them landing first,
        // which would reverse them.
        let anchor = tr;
        if (!rows.length) {
            const none = document.createElement('tr');
            none.className = 'task-subrow';
            none.setAttribute('data-depth', String(depth + 1));
            none.innerHTML = '<td colspan="11" class="pm-empty">No sub tasks.</td>';
            anchor.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', none);
        } else {
            for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
                const kid = taskRowEl(rows[i], tabKey, i, depth + 1);
                anchor.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', kid);
                anchor = kid;
            }
        }
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        btn.classList.add('is-open');
        expandedTaskIds.add(String(taskId));
    }

    // The cache is per parent and goes stale the moment anything is
    // written to a sub task -- completing one, closing one, adding one.
    // Called from the places that already refresh the grid, so a
    // re-expand shows what was just done rather than what was fetched
    // before it.
    function invalidateChildRows(taskId) {
        if (taskId === undefined || taskId === null) childRowCache.clear();
        else childRowCache.delete(String(taskId));
    }

    function actionTrigger(tab, index) {
        return '<button type="button" class="pm-action-trigger" data-tab-action="' + escape(tab) + '" data-row-index="' + index + '" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" title="Actions">'
             + '<i class="fas fa-ellipsis-v fa-solid fa-ellipsis-vertical" aria-hidden="true"></i>'
             + '<span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span>'
             + '</button>';
    }
    function formatBadge(v) { return v ? '<span class="pm-badge">' + escape(v) + '</span>' : ''; }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Task Centre v2 cell renderers  (BRD §7, §8, §11, §13, §17)
    //
    // Every one of these degrades to the pre-v2 output when the row does
    // not carry the v2 field, so the grid still renders against a
    // database where migrations 192-195 have not been applied yet.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const SLA_BADGE_STYLE = {
        OnTrack:   { bg: '#dcfce7', fg: '#166534', label: 'On Track'  },
        DueSoon:   { bg: '#fef9c3', fg: '#854d0e', label: 'Due Soon'  },
        DueToday:  { bg: '#ffedd5', fg: '#9a3412', label: 'Due Today' },
        Breached:  { bg: '#fee2e2', fg: '#991b1b', label: 'Breached'  },
        Extended:  { bg: '#e0e7ff', fg: '#3730a3', label: 'Extended'  },
        Completed: { bg: '#f1f5f9', fg: '#475569', label: 'Completed' },
        NotSet:    { bg: '#f1f5f9', fg: '#64748b', label: 'No SLA'    }
    };

    function fmtDate(v) {
        if (!v) return '';
        // Project-wide date format (dd-MMM-yyyy, +HH:mm when a real time is
        // present). gracFormatDisplayDate returns the value unchanged when it
        // is not a date; only then fall back to the old yyyy-MM-dd slice.
        if (typeof window.gracFormatDisplayDate === 'function') {
            const out = window.gracFormatDisplayDate(v);
            if (out !== v) return out;
        }
        const d = new Date(v);
        return isNaN(d.getTime()) ? String(v).slice(0, 10) : d.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
    }

    function slaStatusBadge(r) {
        const code = r.slaStatusCode;
        if (!code) return r.isOverdue ? '<span class="pm-badge">Breached</span>' : '';
        const s = SLA_BADGE_STYLE[code] || { bg: '#f1f5f9', fg: '#475569', label: code };
        return '<span class="pm-badge" style="background:' + s.bg + '; color:' + s.fg + ';">'
             + escape(s.label) + '</span>';
    }

    // BRD §8: the standard due date is never destroyed by an approved
    // extension, so when one exists we show both — the effective date
    // the task is now monitored against, and the original commitment.
    function dueCell(r) {
        const effective = fmtDate(r.slaDueAt);
        if (!r.isExtended || !r.standardDueAt) return escape(effective);
        return escape(effective)
             + '<div style="font-size:11px; color:#64748b;">std ' + escape(fmtDate(r.standardDueAt)) + '</div>';
    }

    // BRD §12: "Completion of a Child Task does not complete the Parent
    // Task." The badge shows remaining mandatory children so the owner
    // can see at a glance why Complete is blocked.
    function childCell(r) {
        const total = r.childCount || 0;
        if (r.isChild) {
            // No longer "child of T-4-91". A sub task now only ever
            // appears indented beneath its own parent row, so naming the
            // parent again in a column is repeating what the tree
            // already says. What the reader cannot see from the indent is
            // whether this one BLOCKS the parent -- BRD §12: only
            // mandatory sub tasks do -- so that is what the cell says.
            return r.isMandatoryChild === false
                ? '<span class="task-sub-tag is-optional">Optional</span>'
                : '<span class="task-sub-tag is-mandatory">Mandatory</span>';
        }
        if (!total) return '';
        const open = r.mandatoryChildOpenCount || 0;
        const done = (r.mandatoryChildCount || 0) - open;
        return escape(done + '/' + (r.mandatoryChildCount || 0))
             + (open === 0 ? ' <span class="pm-badge" style="background:#dcfce7; color:#166534;">Ready</span>' : '');
    }

    function ownerCell(r) {
        if (r.assignedToEmployeeName) {
            const src = r.ownerSourceCode && r.ownerSourceCode !== 'EXPLICIT_SOURCE' && r.ownerSourceCode !== 'REASSIGNED'
                ? '<div style="font-size:11px; color:#64748b;">' + escape(ownerSourceLabel(r.ownerSourceCode)) + '</div>'
                : '';
            return escape(r.assignedToEmployeeName) + src;
        }
        if (r.assignedToEmployeeId) return escape(r.assignedToEmployeeId);
        return '<span style="color:#b45309;">Unassigned</span>';
    }

    function ownerSourceLabel(code) {
        return ({
            PRACTICE_OWNER: 'from Practice owner',
            CONTROL_OWNER:  'from Control owner',
            PROCESS_OWNER:  'from Process owner',
            FUNCTION_OWNER: 'from Function owner',
            ORG_DEFAULT:    'org default owner',
            MANUAL:         'manual assignment'
        })[code] || '';
    }

    // In-flight governance requests (BRD §7, §8) — the operator must be
    // able to see that a decision is parked without opening the task.
    // Migration 255. Source on top, task type underneath: the type used
    // to BE the tab, so with the tabs gone the row is the only place it
    // can live. A task with no source_type_code (pre-192 rows) shows its
    // type alone rather than an empty cell.
    // Migration 256: rebuild the Source options with a count each, the
    // way Gap Centre's filter already did. The whole vocabulary is
    // returned including zeroes -- filtering to Event Assurance and
    // seeing "(0)" tells you something; not finding it in the list does
    // not. Selection is preserved across the rebuild.
    async function loadTaskSourceFilter() {
        const sel = document.getElementById('taskFilterSource');
        if (!sel || !selectedOrgId) return;
        const keep = sel.value || '';
        try {
            const r = await fetch(
                U('/practice/api/tasks/source-counts?organizationId=') + encodeURIComponent(selectedOrgId),
                { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
            const b = await r.json();
            const rows = (b && b.sources) || [];
            // No rows means the count procedure is missing or failed.
            // Leave the static options in place -- an unlabelled filter
            // still filters; an emptied one cannot.
            if (!rows.length) return;

            sel.innerHTML = '';
            const all = document.createElement('option');
            all.value = '';
            all.textContent = 'All sources (' + (b.totalCount || 0) + ')';
            sel.appendChild(all);

            rows.forEach(function (row) {
                const code = row.sourceTypeCode || row.SourceTypeCode || '';
                if (!code) return;
                const opt = document.createElement('option');
                opt.value = code;
                opt.textContent = (TASK_SOURCE_LABELS[code] || code)
                                + ' (' + (row.taskCount || row.TaskCount || 0) + ')';
                sel.appendChild(opt);
            });

            // Tasks with no source at all are counted but cannot be
            // filtered to -- sp_task_list has no way to ask for "source
            // is null". Shown as a disabled note so the numbers add up
            // instead of looking like they are missing rows.
            const unsourced = b.unsourcedCount || 0;
            if (unsourced > 0) {
                const opt = document.createElement('option');
                opt.value = '';
                opt.disabled = true;
                opt.textContent = '— ' + unsourced + ' with no source recorded';
                sel.appendChild(opt);
            }
            sel.value = keep;
            if (sel.value !== keep) sel.value = '';
        } catch (err) {
            console.error('task-center: source counts failed', err);
        }
    }

    function sourceCell(r) {
        const code  = r.sourceTypeCode || '';
        const label = TASK_SOURCE_LABELS[code] || code;
        const type  = r.taskTypeName || r.taskTypeCode || '';
        return (label ? '<span class="pm-badge">' + escape(label) + '</span>' : '')
             + (type  ? '<div style="font-size:11px; color:#64748b;">' + escape(type) + '</div>' : '');
    }

    function pendingBadges(r) {
        let out = '';
        if (r.extensionStatusCode === 'Pending')
            out += ' <span class="pm-badge" style="background:#fef9c3; color:#854d0e;">Extension pending</span>';
        if (r.priorityChangeStatusCode === 'Pending')
            out += ' <span class="pm-badge" style="background:#fef9c3; color:#854d0e;">Priority '
                 + escape(r.requestedPriority || '') + ' pending</span>';
        return out;
    }
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Pager
    //
    // Both tabs delegate to the shared implementation in
    // _workflow-common.cshtml. This screen still owns pagesByTab -- each
    // tab remembers its own page across tab switches -- and only reports
    // the direction; the helper owns the label, the row range and the
    // Prev/Next disabling.
    //
    // The old local copy incremented past the last page with no bound,
    // and dereferenced [data-pg="prev"] without a null check.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function wirePagers() {
        const wf = window.__wfCommon;
        if (!wf) { console.error('__wfCommon missing - _workflow-common partial not rendered'); return; }
        document.querySelectorAll('.pm-pager').forEach(function (nav) {
            const tab = nav.getAttribute('data-pager');
            if (!tab) return;
            wf.wirePager(tab, function (delta) {
                const target = (pagesByTab[tab] || 1) + delta;
                if (target < 1) return;
                pagesByTab[tab] = target;
                reloadCurrentTab();
            });
        });
    }
    function updatePager(tab, payload) {
        const wf = window.__wfCommon;
        if (!wf) return;
        const rows = (payload && payload.rows) || [];
        wf.updatePager(tab, Object.assign({}, payload, {
            pageSize: PAGE_SIZE,
            rowCount: rows.length
        }));
    }
    function escape(v) {
        if (v === null || v === undefined) return '';
        return String(v).replace(/[&<>"']/g, function (c) {
            return { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;' }[c];
        });
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Row 3-dot menu
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function closeRowMenu() {
        if (openMenuEl)      { openMenuEl.remove(); openMenuEl = null; }
        if (openMenuTrigger) { openMenuTrigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false'); openMenuTrigger = null; }
    }
    function positionRowMenu(trigger) {
        if (!openMenuEl) return;
        const r  = trigger.getBoundingClientRect();
        const mr = openMenuEl.getBoundingClientRect();
        const gap = 6;
        let top = r.bottom + gap, left = r.right - mr.width;
        if (top + mr.height > window.innerHeight - 8) top = Math.max(8, r.top - mr.height - gap);
        if (left < 8) left = 8;
        if (left + mr.width > window.innerWidth - 8) left = window.innerWidth - mr.width - 8;
        openMenuEl.style.top = top + 'px';
        openMenuEl.style.left = left + 'px';
    }
    // =================================================================
    // THREE STATES, NOT TWO.
    //
    // The menu answers "what can I do with this row right now?", and that
    // question has three answers, not two:
    //
    //   applicable: false   This action can NEVER apply to this item.
    //                       Completing a task that is already closed;
    //                       giving a sub task its own sub tasks. HIDDEN --
    //                       a permanently grey row is noise that the
    //                       reader has to re-evaluate every time.
    //
    //   disabled + reason   Applicable, but blocked BY SOMETHING THAT CAN
    //                       CHANGE. Mandatory sub tasks still open; the
    //                       analysis not finished yet. SHOWN and greyed,
    //                       because the reader needs to know the action
    //                       exists and what would unblock it.
    //
    //   (neither)           Available now.
    //
    // The distinction is roughly: a TERMINAL or STRUCTURAL fact hides;
    // an unmet PREREQUISITE disables. Both were previously collapsed into
    // `disabled`, so a closed task showed seven grey rows that would never
    // become anything else.
    //
    // NOTE ON AUTHORITY: this is presentation only. Every rule mirrored
    // here is also enforced by the API and by SQL -- sp_task_complete's
    // §12 gate, sp_task_update's closed-task refusal, the state machine.
    // Hiding an item removes a button, never a check.
    // =================================================================
    function openRowMenu(trigger, items) {
        closeRowMenu();
        openMenuTrigger = trigger;
        trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        openMenuEl = document.createElement('div');
        openMenuEl.className = 'pm-action-menu';
        openMenuEl.setAttribute('role', 'menu');

        const shown = items.filter(function (it) { return it && it.applicable !== false; });

        if (!shown.length) {
            // Better than an empty popover: says the row is read-only
            // rather than looking like a rendering fault.
            const p = document.createElement('div');
            p.className = 'pm-action-menu-empty';
            p.style.cssText = 'padding:8px 12px; font-size:12px; color:#94a3b8; white-space:nowrap;';
            p.textContent = 'No actions available';
            openMenuEl.appendChild(p);
        }

        for (const it of shown) {
            const b = document.createElement('button');
            b.type = 'button'; b.setAttribute('role', 'menuitem');
            b.innerHTML = '<i class="fa-solid ' + escape(it.icon) + '" aria-hidden="true"></i> ' + escape(it.label);
            if (it.disabled) {
                b.disabled = true;
                b.title = it.disabledReason || '';
                // A greyed item that cannot say why is a dead end. Caught
                // here so it shows up in development rather than as a
                // silent shrug in production.
                if (!it.disabledReason) {
                    console.warn('[task-center] menu item "' + it.label
                               + '" is disabled with no reason. Either give it a disabledReason'
                               + ' or mark it applicable:false so it is hidden.');
                }
            }
            b.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
                closeRowMenu();
                try { it.action(); } catch (err) { console.error('[task-center] menu action failed', err); }
            });
            openMenuEl.appendChild(b);
        }
        document.body.appendChild(openMenuEl);
        positionRowMenu(trigger);
    }
    function buildRowMenu(tr) {
        // Candidate rows are a different entity with a different verb set
        // (validate / approve / discard, not assign / transition / close),
        // so they get their own builder rather than a pile of branches.
        if (tr.hasAttribute('data-candidate-id')) return buildCandidateRowMenu(tr);

        // Gap-row branch removed — Implementation gap rows now live in
        // Gap Center (Views/Practice/Partials/gaps.cshtml) which builds
        // its own 3-dot menu with View Practice Instance / Add
        // Implementation Task / View Existing Tasks.
        const taskId      = tr.getAttribute('data-task-id');
        const isTerminal  = tr.getAttribute('data-task-terminal') === '1';
        const isChild     = tr.getAttribute('data-task-child') === '1';
        const isEligible  = tr.getAttribute('data-task-eligible') === '1';
        const taskTitle   = tr.getAttribute('data-task-title') || '';
        const taskNumber  = tr.getAttribute('data-task-number') || ('#' + taskId);
        const taskType    = tr.getAttribute('data-task-type') || '';

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        // The item list itself -- what shows, what is hidden, what is
        // shown-but-disabled-with-a-reason -- now comes from the SHARED
        // window.gracTaskActions.buildMenu(), not from a copy of this
        // logic. Task View's own "Actions" menu builds from the same
        // function with the same fields, so both screens agree on
        // permission and applicability rules by construction rather than
        // by two implementations happening to match. See
        // wwwroot/js/Shared/task-actions.js for the rules themselves
        // (unchanged from what used to live directly in this function --
        // BRD §7, §8, §11, §12, §16) and for why each dialog
        // (Edit / Complete / Close / Add Evidence) is opened through
        // window.gracTaskActions rather than a local function.
        //
        // "View" stays a LOCAL handler: it is the one item Task Center
        // still owns outright, since it navigates to the dedicated Task
        // View page rather than opening a shared dialog. "Add Child
        // Task" also stays local -- openAddChildTask() below -- because
        // it already had its own shared component (window.gracTaskForm)
        // before this change and did not need to move again.
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------
        return window.gracTaskActions.buildMenu(
            { taskId: taskId, taskNumber: taskNumber, taskTitle: taskTitle, taskType: taskType,
              isTerminal: isTerminal, isChild: isChild, isEligible: isEligible },
            {
                onView: function () {
                    window.location.href = U('/Practice/Index/task-view') + '?taskId=' + encodeURIComponent(taskId);
                },
                onEdit:        function () { window.gracTaskActions.openEdit(taskId); },
                onComplete:    function () { window.gracTaskActions.openComplete(taskId, taskNumber, taskTitle); },
                onAddChild:    function () { openAddChildTask(taskId); },
                onAddEvidence: function () { window.gracTaskActions.openEvidenceUpload(taskId, taskNumber); },
                onAddUpdate:   function () { window.gracTaskActions.openAddUpdate(taskId); },
                // Both flags are false in window.gracTaskActions.FLAGS today,
                // so buildMenu() never shows these two -- the handlers are
                // supplied anyway so the item appears automatically, with
                // zero further code changes here, the day either flag flips.
                onViewAssuranceActivity: function () { /* wired when Assurance drill-down lands */ },
                onViewWorkflowHistory:   function () { /* wired when workflow-history viewer lands */ },
                onClose:       function () { window.gracTaskActions.openClose(taskId, taskNumber, taskTitle); }
            }
        );
    }
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Shared org-employees fetch — used by Validate Candidate below.
    // (Task Edit's own copy of this now lives in the shared
    // window.gracTaskActions module alongside the rest of the Edit
    // dialog -- this one stays local because Task Candidates are their
    // own screen, unrelated to the Task View / Task Center Actions-menu
    // change, and were not touched by it.)
    // Hits the existing /practice/api/organizations/{id}/employees endpoint.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    async function fetchOrgEmployees(orgId) {
        if (!orgId) return [];
        const url = U('/practice/api/organizations/') + encodeURIComponent(orgId) + '/employees';
        const r = await fetch(url, { credentials: 'same-origin' });
        if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status + ' from ' + url);
        const arr = await r.json();
        return Array.isArray(arr) ? arr : [];
    }
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Task Candidate row menu + actions  (BRD §5)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function buildCandidateRowMenu(tr) {
        const id      = tr.getAttribute('data-candidate-id');
        const ready   = tr.getAttribute('data-candidate-ready') === '1';
        const priority = tr.getAttribute('data-candidate-priority') || '';

        return [
            { icon: 'fa-eye', label: 'View',
                action: function () { openCandidateView(id); } },

            { icon: 'fa-user-check', label: 'Validate (owner / priority)',
                action: function () { openValidateCandidate(id, priority); } },

            // DISABLED, not hidden, and deliberately so: approving is
            // exactly what this candidate is for, and the only thing in
            // the way is a prerequisite the reader can go and satisfy
            // with the Validate action directly above. Hiding it would
            // remove the signpost pointing at what to do next.
            { icon: 'fa-circle-check', label: 'Approve → create task',
                disabled: !ready,
                disabledReason: 'A confirmed owner is required before a candidate can become an accountable task. Use Validate first.',
                action: function () { approveCandidate(id); } },

            { icon: 'fa-ban', label: 'Discard',
                action: function () { discardCandidate(id); } }
        ];
    }

    async function postCandidateAction(id, path, payload, okMessage) {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U('/practice/api/task-candidates/') + encodeURIComponent(id) + path, {
                method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                credentials: 'same-origin', body: JSON.stringify(payload || {})
            });
            const b = await r.json().catch(function () { return {}; });
            if (r.ok) {
                if (okMessage) alert(typeof okMessage === 'function' ? okMessage(b) : okMessage);
                reloadCurrentTab();
                refreshCounts();
                return true;
            }
            alert((b.error || 'Request failed') + (b.reasonCode ? '\n[' + b.reasonCode + ']' : ''));
            return false;
        } catch (err) {
            alert('Network error: ' + err.message);
            return false;
        }
    }

    async function openCandidateView(id) {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U('/practice/api/task-candidates/') + encodeURIComponent(id), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status);
            const d = await r.json();
            const h = d && d.header;
            if (!h) { alert('Candidate not found.'); return; }
            alert((h.candidateNumber || ('Candidate #' + h.taskCandidateId))
                + '\n\n' + (h.candidateTitle || '')
                + '\n\nSource:   ' + (h.sourceReference || h.sourceTypeCode) + ' #' + h.sourceRecordId
                + '\nStatus:   ' + h.statusCode
                + '\nOwner:    ' + (h.proposedOwnerName || '— not resolved —')
                + (h.ownerSourceCode ? ' (' + h.ownerSourceCode + ')' : '')
                + '\nPriority: ' + h.proposedPriority
                + '\nSLA:      ' + (h.proposedSlaDays != null ? h.proposedSlaDays + ' days' : '—')
                + '  due ' + (fmtDate(h.proposedDueAt) || '—')
                + (h.approvedTaskId ? '\n\nApproved as task ' + (h.approvedTaskNumber || h.approvedTaskId) : '')
                + (h.discardReason ? '\n\nDiscarded: ' + h.discardReason : ''));
        } catch (err) { alert('Load failed: ' + err.message); }
    }

    // BRD §5: the candidate stage confirms owner and priority, nothing
    // more. Priority is freely settable here — the §7 asymmetry (increase
    // free, reduction approved) only starts once a commitment exists.
    async function openValidateCandidate(id, currentPriority) {
        const emps = await fetchOrgEmployees(selectedOrgId).catch(function () { return []; });
        const owner = await window.gracUi.prompt('Confirm the owner. Options: '
            + emps.map(function (e) { return e.employeeId + ' — ' + e.employeeName; }).join('; ')
            + '. Enter employee id (blank = leave unchanged):',
            { title: 'Validate candidate #' + id, inputLabel: 'Employee id', confirmText: 'Continue' });
        if (owner === null) return;

        const priority = await window.gracUi.prompt('Current: ' + (currentPriority || 'Medium')
            + '. The SLA is derived from this and cannot be typed in. '
            + 'Enter Low, Medium, High or Critical (blank = leave unchanged):',
            { title: 'Proposed priority', inputLabel: 'Priority', confirmText: 'Continue' });
        if (priority === null) return;

        const payload = {};
        if (owner && Number(owner.trim()))  payload.proposedOwnerEmployeeId = Number(owner.trim());
        if (priority && priority.trim())    payload.proposedPriority        = priority.trim();
        if (!payload.proposedOwnerEmployeeId && !payload.proposedPriority) return;

        await postCandidateAction(id, '/validate', payload, 'Candidate validated.');
    }

    async function approveCandidate(id) {
        if (!await window.gracUi.confirm('This creates an Approved Task with the confirmed owner '
              + 'and priority, and derives the SLA from the organisation policy in force right now.',
              { title: 'Approve candidate #' + id, confirmText: 'Approve' })) return;
        await postCandidateAction(id, '/approve', {}, function (b) {
            return 'Task ' + (b.approvedTaskId || '?') + ' created from this candidate.';
        });
    }

    async function discardCandidate(id) {
        const reason = await window.gracUi.prompt(
            'The source record is NOT closed or changed — only this proposed task is dropped.',
            { type: 'warning', title: 'Discard candidate #' + id,
              inputLabel: 'Reason', confirmText: 'Discard' });
        if (!reason || !reason.trim()) return;
        await postCandidateAction(id, '/discard', { discardReason: reason.trim() }, 'Candidate discarded.');
    }

    function wireRowMenu() {
        const root = document.getElementById('taskCenterRoot');
        if (root) {
            root.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                // The sub-task toggle shares this one delegated listener
                // rather than being bound per row: the grid is rebuilt on
                // every page, filter and search change, and per-row
                // listeners would have to be rebound each time -- the
                // same reasoning the row menu is delegated for.
                const expander = e.target.closest('.task-tree-toggle[data-task-expand]');
                if (expander && root.contains(expander)) {
                    e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
                    closeRowMenu();          // it is anchored to a row that is about to move
                    toggleTaskRow(expander);
                    return;
                }
                const trigger = e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger');
                if (trigger && root.contains(trigger)) {
                    e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
                    const tr = trigger.closest('tr');
                    if (!tr) return;
                    if (openMenuTrigger === trigger) { closeRowMenu(); return; }
                    openRowMenu(trigger, buildRowMenu(tr));
                    return;
                }
                // Row click-to-View (change request, 2026-09-22): a task
                // row (parent or sub task alike) opens Task View, exactly
                // what its own "View" menu item does; a candidate row
                // opens its quick-look modal instead (buildCandidateRowMenu's
                // own View item, openCandidateView) -- neither has an
                // in-row link today, but !e.target.closest('a') is kept
                // for the same reason the other screens keep it.
                const tr = e.target.closest('tr.pm-row-clickable');
                if (!tr || !root.contains(tr) || e.target.closest('a')) return;
                if (tr.hasAttribute('data-candidate-id')) {
                    openCandidateView(tr.getAttribute('data-candidate-id'));
                } else if (tr.hasAttribute('data-task-id')) {
                    window.location.href = U('/Practice/Index/task-view')
                        + '?taskId=' + encodeURIComponent(tr.getAttribute('data-task-id'));
                }
            });
        }
        document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            if (!openMenuEl) return;
            if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-menu')) return;
            if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger')) return;
            closeRowMenu();
        });
        document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) { if (e.key === 'Escape') closeRowMenu(); });
        window.addEventListener('resize', closeRowMenu);
        window.addEventListener('scroll',  closeRowMenu, true);
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Row-menu action helpers
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Task detail view  (BRD §16)
    //
    // Replaces the previous alert() stub. One call to
    // GET /practice/api/tasks/{id} returns header + activity + evidence
    // + children + governance requests, so the drawer never fans out
    // into five round trips.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------

    // BRD §7: increases apply immediately; reductions need an approved
    // Exception. The prompt spells that out so nobody is surprised when
    // "High → Medium" does not take effect.

    // BRD §8: an extension is a request, never an override. The date does
    // not move until Exception Centre approves.

    // "Add Sub Task" from a task's row menu.
    //
    // This was FOUR chained window.prompt() boxes and a confirm(): title,
    // then a newline-joined employee list to read an id out of, then
    // mandatory-or-not. It could not show which task it was adding to, it
    // had no validation, and an employee id had to be typed by hand.
    //
    // The parent is known here -- it is the row the menu was opened on --
    // so the common form is opened with it fixed and read-only. The user
    // is never asked to choose a parent they already chose.
    async function openAddChildTask(parentTaskId) {
        const orgSel = document.getElementById('taskFilterOrganization');
        const orgName = (orgSel && orgSel.options[orgSel.selectedIndex]
                         && orgSel.options[orgSel.selectedIndex].textContent) || null;

        // Title and number for the read-only Parent Task field, taken from
        // the row already on screen -- no round trip to name a task the
        // user is looking at.
        const tr = document.querySelector('tr[data-task-id="' + parentTaskId + '"]');
        const parent = {
            taskId: Number(parentTaskId),
            taskNumber: tr ? (tr.getAttribute('data-task-number') || null) : null,
            title: tr ? (tr.getAttribute('data-task-title') || null) : null
        };

        window.gracTaskForm.open({
            mode: 'subtask',
            organizationId: Number(selectedOrgId),
            organizationName: orgName,
            parentTask: parent,
            onSaved: function () { refreshCounts(); reloadCurrentTab(); }
        });
    }

    // BRD §12: the parent owner confirms completion of the overall
    // objective — completion is never implied by the last child closing.


    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // New Task (Custom) dialog wiring
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Both entry points now open THE common Task / Sub Task form
    // (Shared/task-form.js + _task-form-dialog.cshtml). The Task Center
    // no longer owns a task form of its own -- the layout in the
    // screenshot moved into the shared partial unchanged, so this screen
    // looks identical while every other screen gets the same thing.
    function openNewTaskDialog() {
        if (!selectedOrgId) {
            alert('Select an organization first — the Assigned To dropdown scopes to that organization.');
            return;
        }
        const orgSel = document.getElementById('taskFilterOrganization');
        const orgName = (orgSel && orgSel.options[orgSel.selectedIndex]
                         && orgSel.options[orgSel.selectedIndex].textContent) || null;
        window.gracTaskForm.open({
            mode: 'task',
            organizationId: Number(selectedOrgId),
            organizationName: orgName,
            onSaved: function () { refreshCounts(); reloadCurrentTab(); }
        });
    }
})();
</script>

